    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s July 20th slate, the premier play is **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81), who leverages a favorable matchup against Springs to anchor the lineup, bolstered by an excellent spot in the two-hole. **Cal Raleigh** (71.45) and **Daulton Varsho** (69.27) follow closely, both capitalizing on plus-matchups against pitchers with elevated expected ERAs. **Luis Arraez** (67.03) and **Taylor Ward** (64.61) are also locked in as high-floor contributors, with both benefitting from premium leadoff positioning that maximizes their opportunities to score runs\u2014a critical factor for our 5x5 Roto standing.\n\nThe primary bench dilemma today involved **Tyler Freeman**, who nearly cracked the lineup with a 52.57 score driven by a significant park factor (+14%). However, he ultimately fell short because his efficiency metrics were suppressed by an unfavorable draw against Alvarez and a low-leverage spot in the eight-hole, leaving him on the outside looking in behind higher-projected starters like **Masyn Winn**. While **Jonathan Aranda** was also considered, his date with the elite arm of Cease (2.96 xERA) rendered him a suboptimal start despite his strong dynamic platoon profile.\n\nLooking across the roster, we are leaning into aggressive platoon edges, most notably with **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Daulton Varsho**, both receiving double-digit boosts due to their favorable matchups against right-handed pitching. **Gleyber Torres** remains a start despite some platoon regression risk, as he gains value from a wind-aided environment that should help his power profile. We are monitoring **Bryce Harper** closely; while his 61.77 score is solid, he faces a moderate test against Sheehan, so we are keeping a close eye on his xwOBA consistency throughout the game to ensure he maintains his expected production level.",
